From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:04:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] output: Tell the light sensor what the panel shows over it

Plinius: the light sensor sits behind the OLED panel and sees its light.
Its firmware takes that off, from the brightness and from the colour
shown over the sensor, which the system has to tell it. Without that a
white page read as a brighter room and a black one as a darker room,
and auto brightness followed the picture.

An output can now have a light sensor in phoc.ini: the part of the
screen it sees (light-sensor = x,y,width,height in buffer pixels), how
much each cell of a grid over that part counts (light-sensor-weights,
rows separated by ";") and the colour value its firmware wants for full
white (light-sensor-gain). After a frame whose damage touches that
part, phoc reads it back, at most four times a second, averages it in
linear light with the weights and writes the colour in the driver's own
format to $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/plinius-als-color. When a client's buffer is
scanned out directly nothing is read, the file goes and the device's
default applies.
